lready, haven't you?"JWell then it can't be helped. We might as well make use of your help."aOk then... What I'm about to tell you is highly classified information, so listen carefully."fThe crater you see here was made by a strange object that fell out of the sky a few nights ago..."uAt first we believed that it was a meteor, but this object's composition is unlike any meteor we've seen before."ZAfter running some tests on it, we now believe that it is part of an alien spaceship."8I know... It's hard to believe, but it's the truth!"�But this is just some debris so it's no use to us at the moment. However, we believe that the rest of the ship might've fallen elsewhere."lAccording to witnesses, the ship burst into three separate parts shortly after entering the atmosphere."�We've been unable to locate the other two pieces so far, but we believe that one of them might be the spaceship's main component."~One meteor was reported in the \C[3]Johto region\C[0], \C[1]East of Goldenrod City\C[0] around the same time as this one."]Another one was reported in the \C[5]Kanto region\C[0], \C[1]South of Fuchsia City.\C[0]"ZWe need you to go investigate these two areas for signs of the ship's main component."ZAnd please be discreet about it. Remember that all of this is classified information!"kAccording to witnesses the ship burst into three separate parts shortly after entering the atmosphere."eSo you've been able to locate the impact points of the other two meteors? That's fantastic news!"�Hmm... But it seems like these Spaceship Parts you found are nothing but debris. We're no closer to finding the ship's main component."SAghh! To think we've come so far just to find ourselves in another dead-end..."Unless..."�That's it! Using the positions from the three meteors' impact points, I should be able to triangulate the main ship's coordinates!""Give me a few seconds here..."xSorry to keep you waiting. If my calculations are correct the alien spaceship should be at these exact coordinates."'\C[1]\PN memorized the coordinates"GIt seems like it's not too far off the coast from Cinnabar Island."}And according to our GPS data, there's a small, uncharted island at these same coordinates. This could be our lucky day!"�\PN, I need you to ask the man at Cinnabar Island's harbour to take you to this uncharted island and to report back with what you find there. Understood?"WIf my calculations are correct the alien spaceship should be at these coordinates."�And according to our GPS data, there's a small, uncharted island located at these same coordinates so this could be our lucky day!"�I need you to ask the man at Cinnabar Island's harbour to take you to this uncharted island and to report back with what you find there. Understood?"&Hey! You better not be littering!"Oh, I see how it is."VWe don't own the planet, we belong to it. And we must share it with our wildlife." Oh, did you want a rematch?"Gobble!"3We're here as we promised... Are you prepared?"EI'll come at you with all I have. As if we were in Olivine City!"Well done..."E...You are a better Trainer than me, in both skill and kindness."JIn accordance with League rules, I confer upon you the Mineral Badge."GI also wanted to give you this Pokémon... For helping me earlier."mIt's a Pokémon that was given to me on Chrono Island. When it evolves, its shell will be hard as steel!"q\C[5]Corsola\C[0] also seem to be deathly afraid of it, so it might help you clear some blocked off paths..."9Um... I don't know how to say this, but good luck..."Q16 badges... That is impressive! I'm sure that Professor Oak would be proud!"Um... Take your time..."C...I came from very far away because I wanted to get stronger."~On the way I met all sorts of people with their Pokémon... They all looked like they were having fun. I felt happy seeing it."bThe wild fruits in this route attract a lot of rare Pokémon. We do our best to protect them!"Crikey!"(I punish people who abuse Pokémon!"Oh no!"Shoot!"DI work