!"NIt's located right outside the tunnel, straight ahead, then to the right."oThe Exp. Lab is a high-tech laboratory where they can make \C[1]Experience Candies\C[0] for your Pokémon."yIf you'd like to check it out, it's located on the upper level behind the gym, in the northernmost part of the city."YMost of the region's TV broadcasts are filmed right here at the TV Mauville studios."jThe studios are free to tour! To find it, just take a left in the tunnel and head to the lower level."eMauville is very well known for its Game Corner. People come from all over the region to gamble!"pThe fastest way there is to take the stairs to the lower level of tunnel on the left and then head outside!"sThe Pokéball Workshop is a family-owned workshop that can swap your Pokémon's Pokéball for a different one."YYou can find the workshop by taking a left and heading to the lower level of tunnel."!Do you choose this Pokémon?"(This is the \C[1]Transfer Box\C[0]."�This box can be used to transfer Pokémon between \C[1]Pokémon Infinite Fusion\C[0] and \C[1]Pokémon Infinite Fusion: Hoenn\C[0] or between savefiles."�Any Pokémon that is placed in this box will be accessible from every savefile of either game. You can deposit or withdraw Pokémon just like you would for any other box."Transfer Box"Transfer Box (Off)"�The Transfer Box is disabled because your savefile is flagged as randomized. You can still use it as a normal PC box, but the Pokémon you put in it won't be available in your other savefiles"�\C[2]The Transfer Box is disabled because your savefile is flagged as randomized. You can still use it as a normal PC box, but the Pokémon you put in it won't be available in your other savefiles"cMoving Pokémon in and out of the transfer box will save the game automatically. Is this okay?" You don't have any berries!"%Starting up the Berry Blender..."EPlease select a berry from your bag to put in the Berry Blender."#Do you want to choose a berry?"+Would you like to blend another berr